  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(2-(-2))-(\\frac{8}{3}-(-\\frac{8}{3})) \\\\  & =16-\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
